=== 4. One tutor turn inside the container (OpenAI cascade) ===
Container started with:
$ SOTTO_API_KEY="$(grep '^SOTTO_API_KEY=' apps/server/.env | cut -d= -f2-)" \
  SOTTO_STT_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1 SOTTO_STT_MODEL=whisper-1 \
  SOTTO_LLM_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1 SOTTO_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini \
  SOTTO_TTS_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1 SOTTO_TTS_MODEL=tts-1 \
  docker compose up -d
(key passed only through the shell environment into the container process;
never written to any file in this repo, never printed — verified below)

Port remapped to 8792 for this run (matching the exact port R3-H's original
selfhost-2026-09-05.log used) so the e2e script's own
`voice/ws opened on the self-hosted origin (:8792)` assertion — which
checks for that literal port substring in the observed WebSocket URL, a
pre-existing hardcoded check in apps/client/e2e/self-hosted-voice.mjs, out
of this lane's edit permissions — passes meaningfully instead of false-
failing on an arbitrary remap. Same image, same env, same code path as any
other port.

$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8792/health
{"ok":true,"stt":true,"llm":true,"tts":true,"vad":"energy"}

$ BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8792 SOTTO_BASIC_AUTH_USER=sotto \
  SOTTO_BASIC_AUTH_PASS=demo-only node apps/client/e2e/self-hosted-voice.mjs
(SOTTO_BASIC_AUTH was left unset on the container in this run, so these
credentials are unused/ignored by the server — carried over from R3-H's
invocation shape for consistency, harmless either way)

